**Phase 0 evidence rule:** no capability, security, compliance, residency, availability, recovery, or production-readiness assertion is accepted solely on the basis of prose, configuration intent, or a local demonstration. Each assertion must map to a version-controlled requirement, an exact source/configuration revision, and a reproducible automated or witnessed check. CI/CD run results and deployment evidence must identify the tested commit, environment, inputs, outcome, and artifact reference. If that evidence is absent or stale, mark the assertion **reported**, **unverified**, or **not implemented**—never passed.

**Containment safety invariant:** this baseline authorizes only dual-control approval and cryptographic command delivery. Privileged Windows Filtering Platform/Linux `nftables` host containment and automated threat quarantine remain **DISABLED**. No OS-level isolation or automatic rollback is implemented. Keep enforcement unavailable until Phase 9 implementation, independent verification, operational testing, and signed authorization gates have all passed.

